{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MyCVJBacdUw2zs3rnh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tq3kEr7zSx2giTHxpXeNXe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"When adding the `html` entry to the build, update all three esbuild\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"Attribute names are checked against `_ATTR` (letter, `_` or `:`, then\nletters, digits, `-`, `_`, `:`, `.`); invalid ones are skipped silently,\nnever thrown, since they come from spreads of user data. The regex is\nduplicated in `src/htm.ts` and `src/htm.browser.ts` (separate entries)\nand must stay identical. Any new path that writes an attribute in\neither templater needs the same guard; in the browser, guard before an\neffect is created, not inside `_setAttr`.\n\nWhen adding the `html` entry to the build, update all three esbuild\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n4. Browser spread: done. Guards in `_compArgs`, `_str` and `_bindEl`\n   (create, patch and adopt all go through `_bindEl`). Guarding in\n   `_bindEl` rather than `_setAttr` means no effect is created for an\n   invalid signal-valued attribute. `_bindHost` only writes `key`.\n5. Browser signal attribute with invalid name: test written after the\n   guard existed; verified it fails (setAttribute throws) with the\n   `_bindEl` guard removed and passes with it.\n\nSize: browser templater went 4.56 -> 4.62 kB with the long regex, over\nthe 4.6 kB limit. Shortened to the equivalent `/^[a-z_:][-\\w:.]*$/i`\nin both templaters; now 4.6 kB, exactly at the limit with no headroom.\nLimit not raised. Later tickets touching htm.browser.ts will likely\nneed to raise it (spec: measured size rounded up to next 0.05 kB).\n\nTests: npm test 294/294, test:ssr 82/82, lint clean, size passes.\nEOF\ngit add -A src test AGENTS.md && git commit -qm \"htm: test signal attributes with invalid names; shorten name regex\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git status --short && git log --oneline -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":83743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441},"output_tokens":49,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24fa634b-341c-42ab-bcd7-195dbd625da7","uuid":"3b11272e-b639-485b-a87a-fede556b8172","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:06:11.731Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MyCEfat76VPTQDgkNQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Tq3kEr7zSx2giTHxpXeNXe":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/microtags.millitags-lessons-02-templaters-skip-invalid-attribute-names && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"When adding the `html` entry to the build, update all three esbuild\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"Attribute names are checked against `_ATTR` (letter, `_` or `:`, then\nletters, digits, `-`, `_`, `:`, `.`); invalid ones are skipped silently,\nnever thrown, since they come from spreads of user data. The regex is\nduplicated in `src/htm.ts` and `src/htm.browser.ts` (separate entries)\nand must stay identical. Any new path that writes an attribute in\neither templater needs the same guard; in the browser, guard before an\neffect is created, not inside `_setAttr`.\n\nWhen adding the `html` entry to the build, update all three esbuild\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n4. Browser spread: done. Guards in `_compArgs`, `_str` and `_bindEl`\n   (create, patch and adopt all go through `_bindEl`). Guarding in\n   `_bindEl` rather than `_setAttr` means no effect is created for an\n   invalid signal-valued attribute. `_bindHost` only writes