{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MytuAbp3RH178mPPLu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Browser suite: a signal-valued attribute with an invalid name is never written on re-render.\n\nBoth templaters now silently drop any attribute key that isn't a valid HTML attribute name. A spread like `{ 'x\" onload=\"alert(1)': 'v' }` no longer escapes the tag on the server or makes `setAttribute` throw in the browser. All five checklist items are done. `npm test` (294 tests), `npm run test:ssr` (82), lint and the size check all pass.\n\n**Where the check sits:**\n- **Server (`src/htm.ts`):** in `h`, for plain elements and for a component's extra attributes. A bad key on a component is filtered out before the component's render is called, so it never reaches the host tag.\n- **Browser (`src/htm.browser.ts`):** in `_str` (the `String()` path), `_compArgs` and `_bindEl`. Create, patch and adopt all go through `_bindEl`. The ticket named `_setAttr`, but I put the check in `_bindEl` so that no update effect is ever set up for a signal bound to a bad name.\n\n**Size:** the browser templater is now exactly at its 4.6 kB limit, with no room left. My first version put it 16 B over (it was 4.56 kB before). Rather than raise the limit, I switched both templaters to a shorter regex that matches the same names, `/^[a-z_:][-\\w:.]*$/i`. The next ticket that touches `src/htm.browser.ts` (probably item 3 or 5) will likely have to raise the limit.\n\n**Tests:**\n- The \"static pages stay byte-identical\" item needed no new test, because the existing \"static page output is unchanged\" test still passes.\n- The re-render test passed as soon as I wrote it, because the `_bindEl` check was already in place from the previous item. To make sure it can fail, I removed that check temporarily: the test failed, then passed once I put the check back.\n\nI added a short note to `AGENTS.md`: the regex is duplicated in the two templaters and must stay identical, and any new code that writes attributes needs the same check. My notes for this ticket are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which isn't committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1043,"cache_read_input_tokens":84184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1043},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24fa634b-341c-42ab-bcd7-195dbd625da7","uuid":"3b02621b-a89b-4526-a2fe-551642d33bde","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:06:19.942Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Myte2xRVF5KTxbxNJg"}
